<linker>
  <!--
    Engine classes reached ONLY from code. "Strip Engine Code" keeps a native class when a scene
    or asset in the build carries it; one that exists solely as an AddComponent<T>() call is
    dropped, and the call then returns null on a device while working in the Editor. The log line
    is: AddComponent asking for "SpriteMask" which is not a Unity engine type.

    SpriteMask: PortraitCastEffect, the hero power cast. This keeps the managed wrapper.
    Unity 6000.6 also needs com.unity.modules.tilemap enabled to retain the native class
    (UUM-138419); scene references and link.xml alone do not prevent its removal.
    Retire that module workaround after upgrading to a Unity version with the fix.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="UnityEngine.SpriteMaskModule">
    <type fullname="UnityEngine.SpriteMask" preserve="all"/>
  </assembly>
  <!--
    The colliders GameObject.CreatePrimitive adds. Nothing in a scene carries a CapsuleCollider,
    so a device build stripped it and CreatePrimitive(Cylinder) logged "Can't add component
    because class 'CapsuleCollider' doesn't exist!", which took The Spark coin, and with it the
    whole match wiring, down on 0.0.10 (2026-10-19). Kept for every shape the code creates.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="UnityEngine.PhysicsModule">
    <type fullname="UnityEngine.CapsuleCollider" preserve="all"/>
    <type fullname="UnityEngine.BoxCollider" preserve="all"/>
    <type fullname="UnityEngine.MeshCollider" preserve="all"/>
    <type fullname="UnityEngine.SphereCollider" preserve="all"/>
  </assembly>
</linker>
